      "Language": "ukr",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Submitted in the paper are results of studies on gastrocepin effects on degree of clinical symptoms, contractility of the gall bladder, and power of the threshold load in patients with ischemic heart disease and disordered motor function of the bile tracts. Gastrocepin is shown to increase contractility of the gall bladder and facilitate normalization of the Oddie's sphincter tone; it makes for the reduction in the incidence of anginal attacks and increase in the physical exercise tolerance in patients with stabile functional class I and II angina pectoris of effort."},
